# Woman silhouettes only

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`) whenever a **silhouette** is used — section tiles, cards, backgrounds, collages, mocks.

Diana is a woman and must be able to relate to the figure.

## Always

- If you use a human silhouette, it must clearly read as a **woman** (feminine hair/shape/pose — long or curly hair, dress, etc.)
- Prefer the same scene/mood she already liked, but swap gender of the figure if the prior one was masculine or ambiguous
- Keep `everything.html` + `prototype.html` (+ `serve.py` when photos change) in sync

## Never

- Masculine or gender-ambiguous human silhouettes
- “Lone figure” stock that reads as a man (short hair, broad shoulders) for detach or any other focus
- Restoring `zone-detach-silhouette.jpg` / masculine crescent-moon figure once banned

## Related

- `section-images-real-photography` — **silhouettes are allowed** on section photos when they help the concept; faces / photoreal people are not. **Audacity finger** remains the only approved non-woman silhouette exception (Diana-supplied)
- This rule always applies whenever a silhouette is used: **woman only**
- `no-other-faces-or-names` — still no faces / other people’s names on generated/found images

## If a masculine silhouette is live

Replace it immediately with a clear woman’s silhouette. Do not ask permission.
